# .gitignore for an EcoStruxure Automation Expert (EAE) solution
# Put this file next to the .sln / .nxtsln (the solution root).
# Everything ignored here is regenerated by EAE on Build/Deploy, or is
# installed with EAE itself. What is left is the source: a few MB instead of ~1 GB.

# --- Library copies (the big one, ~1 GB) -----------------------------------
# EAE keeps a copy of every referenced library (.fblib) in the solution.
# They are standard Schneider libraries that ship with EAE and live in
# C:\ProgramData\Schneider Electric\Libraries. Everyone must use the same
# EAE version (library versions are pinned in IEC61499/IEC61499.dfbproj).
.exportedlibraries/
*.fblib

# --- Build output (all projects: IEC61499, HMI, HwConfiguration, ...) -------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# --- Compile snapshots (EAE ships its own .gitignore with "*" here) ---------
**/SnapshotCompiles/

# --- EAE runtime / session files --------------------------------------------
.lock_sln
*.lock
**/System/.obsolete/
log.*.txt
*.log

# --- Solution archives / exports (share these as releases, not in git) ------
*.sln.zip
*.sln.7z
Exports/
Imports/
TestReports/
# Generated help (Build > Generate documentation); EAE also leaves it out of archives.
# solutionlibhelp.help alone is 230 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
Documentation/
*.help

# --- Visual Studio / Windows / editor noise --------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.pdb
*.cache
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
~$*
*.tmp
*.bak

